[39.835, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34m============================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34m  Beat 7\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u00b7 Completeness: what nono alone misses, the gate catches\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34m============================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# This beat deliberately BYPASSES the gate to show nono's raw behaviour, then runs the gate.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# nono is per-file and glob-based: on its own it does not notice a removed file or a type outside\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# its globs. The gate's completeness layer does.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# (a) Remove a signed helper. nono ALONE (gate bypassed) still launches:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.839, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m$ nono run --allow-cwd -- echo WRAPPED_PROCESS_RAN (nono alone, gate bypassed)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
